    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Write these intervals as decimal hours.\n(a) $4$ hours $27$ minutes\n(b) $18$ minutes",
        "solution_text": "(a) $27\\div60=0.45$.\n$4+0.45=4.45$.\nThe interval is $4.45\\text{ h}$.\n(b) $18\\div60=0.3$.\nThe interval is $0.3\\text{ h}$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write these intervals as hours and minutes in part (a), and hours, minutes and seconds in part (b).\n(a) $2.65$ hours\n(b) $3.125$ hours",
        "solution_text": "(a) Keep the $2$ whole hours.\n$0.65\\times60=39$ minutes.\n$2.65\\text{ h}=2\\text{ h }39\\text{ min}$.\n(b) Keep the $3$ whole hours.\n$0.125\\times60=7.5$ minutes.\nKeep the $7$ whole minutes.\n$0.5\\times60=30$ seconds.\n$3.125\\text{ h}=3\\text{ h }7\\text{ min }30\\text{ s}$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Which is longer: $1.45$ hours or $1$ hour $31$ minutes? Give the difference in minutes.\n(b) A student writes $2$ hours $33$ minutes as $2.33$ hours. Explain and correct the error.",
        "solution_text": "(a) $0.45\\times60=27$ minutes.\n$1.45\\text{ h}=1\\text{ h }27\\text{ min}$.\n$31-27=4$ minutes.\n$1\\text{ h }31\\text{ min}$ is longer by $4$ minutes.\n(b) Minutes are parts of an hour with $60$ minutes in the whole hour, not $100$.\n$33\\div60=0.55$.\n$2\\text{ h }33\\text{ min}=2.55\\text{ h}$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Write $2$ hours $14$ minutes $24$ seconds as decimal hours.",
        "solution_text": "Convert the seconds to a fraction of a minute.\n$24\\div60=0.4\\text{ min}$.\nAdd this to the whole minutes.\n$14+0.4=14.4\\text{ min}$.\nConvert the minutes to a fraction of an hour.\n$14.4\\div60=0.24\\text{ h}$.\nAdd the whole hours.\n$2+0.24=2.24\\text{ h}$."
      }
    ],
